Fresh-eyes review complete for `src/blog/people/drafts/Khabib-Nurmagomedov.md`. The notes are appended as a `FRESH EYES REVIEW (2026-08-12)` comment block at the bottom of the file, after the existing ledgers. No body edits were made.

The two biggest issues I flagged:

1. **The mother is a ghost at the center of the piece.** Her word ends the career and explicitly outranks the father's 30-0 wish, but the draft never examines who she is in this system or why her authority won — while the father gets pages of loving detail. Sourcing is thin per the entity-gap packet, but the asymmetry itself is the material: one paragraph reading her invisibility would pay off a contradiction the retirement section currently leaves hanging.

2. **The January 2023 coaching exit that reversed after 17 months is a loose thread that undercuts the thesis.** The piece ends the retirement section on "the unbroken word is the achievement," then quietly notes he announced a full exit from MMA and came back. A skeptical reader will pounce. The fix sharpens the thesis rather than weakening it — a promise given to his mother versus a team statement are different classes of word — but only if the draft draws that line.

Also in the notes: faith is underweighted as the second authority structure (it's what survived the father's death, yet reads as set dressing), two quotes duplicate between the body and the Rabbit Hole, "built a life on it" repeats within one section, and the verdict-cadence section closers are dense enough that the reader starts hearing the template. On the protect list: the cold open (the tears he can't remember) and its "the tape got burned" payoff, the two-Octobers structure, the empathy turn on the fence jump, and the bear-video bookend.
